dates/cfc-iict26/</link><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/cfc-iict26/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Our work, &amp;ldquo;Complementary Function Co-scheduling Across Call Boundaries&amp;rdquo;, has been accepted as a poster at Innovations in Compiler Technology (IICT) Workshop 2026, which will be held at IISc Bengaluru, India, in October 2026.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Conferences</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/conferences/</link><pubDate>Sat, 06 Jun 2026 14:40:59 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/conferences/</guid><description>Snaps from the conferences I have attended: AsiaCCS'26 in Bengaluru and BuildSEC'24 in New Delhi.</description></item><item><title>Attended AsiaCCS 2026 in Bengaluru, India</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/asia-ccs/</link><pubDate>Sat, 06 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/asia-ccs/</guid><description>I attended the AsiaCCS 2026 in Bengaluru, India from 01-05 June 2026, where I had been a volunteer. It was a great experience to attend a flagship security conference in India and interact with the attendees.</description></item><item><title>Misc</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/misc/</link><pubDate>Thu, 12 Feb 2026 14:40:59 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/misc/</guid><description>AI Day 2026 at IIT Gandhinagar, where I presented a poster for our work &amp;ldquo;Davids vs. Goliath — Achieving GPU-like performance using Network of Stations&amp;rdquo;.</description></item><item><title>Presented poster @ AI Day 2026, IITGn</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/ai-day/</link><pubDate>Thu, 12 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/ai-day/</guid><description>I attended the AI Day 2026 at IIT Gandhinagar on 12th February 2026, where I had presented a poster for our work &amp;ldquo;Davids vs. Goliath — Achieving GPU-like performance using Network of Stations&amp;rdquo;.</description></item><item><title>How to Measure Performance of Your Code</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/posts/measure-your-code/</link><pubDate>Fri, 26 Dec 2025 11:30:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/posts/measure-your-code/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Measuring code performance accurately is crucial, especially when optimizing the existing algorithms or designing new ones. In this post, I&amp;rsquo;ll share my learnings of measuring code performance using various tools and techniques.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For measuring execution time, we can use the following techniques:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wall Clock Time (&lt;code&gt;clock_gettime&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linux resource usage metrics (&lt;code&gt;getrusage&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To measure raw Time Stamp Counter (or, ticks), on x86 architectures we can use:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;RDTSC&lt;/code&gt; (Read Time-Stamp Counter)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Finally, to pinpoint performance bottlenecks, we can use the Linux &lt;code&gt;perf&lt;/code&gt; tool; However, there are two ways to use it:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Workshops</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/workshops/</link><pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 14:40:59 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/workshops/</guid><description>Computer Systems Workshop at IISc Bangalore (30–31 October 2025), where I presented a poster.</description></item><item><title>Presented Poster at IISc Bangalore</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/iisc-poster/</link><pubDate>Fri, 31 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/iisc-poster/</guid><description>Presented poster on our work on &amp;ldquo;Accelerating Large Integer Arithmetic with Parallel Addition, Subtraction, and Vedic-Based Multiplication Using AVX512&amp;rdquo; at the Computer Systems Workshop held at IISc Bangalore.</description></item><item><title>Organized Cyber Security CTF at ICAN FDP, IIT Madras</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/ican-ctf/</link><pubDate>Tue, 15 Jul 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/ican-ctf/</guid><description>Organized web security CTFs for ICAN Faculty Development Program on Cybersecurity at IIT Madras.</description></item><item><title>Some memories during my M.Tech at IIT Gandhinagar</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/mtech-memories-iitgn/</link><pubDate>Mon, 30 Jun 2025 10:00:59 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/mtech-memories-iitgn/</guid><description>Some memories from my M.Tech at IIT Gandhinagar: convocation, the Mt. Abu trip, Blithchron'25, and more.</description></item><item><title>IIT Gandhinagar Campus</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/iit-gandhinagar-campus/</link><pubDate>Mon, 03 Feb 2025 14:40:59 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/iit-gandhinagar-campus/</guid><description>The beautiful IIT Gandhinagar campus through my lens, captured during my M.Tech (2023–2025).</description></item><item><title>Teaching</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/teaching/</link><pubDate>Mon, 03 Feb 2025 14:40:59 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/teaching/</guid><description>Student-Run Short Course on Code Profiling and Optimization at IIT Gandhinagar (November 2024), where I was the principal instructor.</description></item><item><title>University of Kalyani</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/university-of-kalyani/</link><pubDate>Mon, 03 Feb 2025 14:40:59 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/gallery/university-of-kalyani/</guid><description>A few shots of my alma mater, the University of Kalyani, taken during my M.Sc (2021–2023).</description></item><item><title>Director's PhD Fellowship</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/phd-fellowship/</link><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/phd-fellowship/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Selected for the &lt;strong&gt;Director&amp;rsquo;s PhD Fellowship&lt;/strong&gt; at the IIT Gandhinagar.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Best Paper Award at BuildSEC'24</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/buildsec-award/</link><pubDate>Fri, 20 Dec 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/updates/buildsec-award/</guid><description>Attended BuildSEC'24 in New Delhi and presented our work on &amp;ldquo;Online Authentication Habits of Indian Users&amp;rdquo;. We also won the Best Paper Award there!</description></item><item><title>Online Authentication Habits of Indian Users</title><link>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/publications/online-authentication-habits/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Dec 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://iitgn-fuss.github.io/people/subhrajit/publications/online-authentication-habits/</guid><description>Pratyush Choudhary, Subhrajit Das, Mukul Paras Potta, Prasuj Das, and Abhishek Bichhawat · BuildSec 2024, New Delhi, India</description></item></channel></rss>